    "answer": {
      "short": "$W=8$",
      "worked": "The subtraction changes both signs in $3(2W-1)$, giving $-6W+3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5(W+4)}{15}-\\frac{3(2W-1)}{15}&=1\\\\\\frac{5W+20-6W+3}{15}&=1\\\\\\frac{23-W}{15}&=1\\\\23-W&=15\\\\23&=15+W\\\\W&=8\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
